FIGURE CELLS, geometry OFF, floor 1e-25 (2026-09-17): ham_ldosonly_n2_L4_nogeom vs blind_dos_L2_nogeom.

Cells scored in this run:
  ham   : <G3NAT_ROOT>/outputs_v3/ham_ldosonly_n2_L4_nogeom_s{seed} / hamiltonian_pickle_model_best.pth (use_geometry=False)
  blind : <G3NAT_ROOT>/outputs_v3/blind_dos_L2_nogeom_s{seed} / standard_pickle_model_best.pth (use_geometry=False)
Default cells (no CLI override) are the v3 DOE pick on l12_transmission (analysis/outputs/doe_v3.out, HEAD-TO-HEAD section): ham=ldosonly_n2_L4_nogeom, blind=tonly_L2_geom.
Per-sequence values are shown at BOTH lengths (L=12 and L=16), not pooled into one row.
n=4 sequences per length. NO interval (confidence interval, error bar, etc.) is claimed at this sample size -- wins/losses and the sign-test p-value only.
Loss = full-curve Huber on log10 T (and, separately, log10 DOS), all 201 energy points, per sequence (mean over its 4 contact variants, then mean over 3 seeds). Lower is better. Both models score DOS regardless of supervision, since forward() always returns a DOS prediction; whether DOS is a trained objective for a given cell is a property of that cell, stated above/by the caller, not of this script.

